ZAICODE

GOAL
Build SAIHOME as ZAICODE's real operator home/dashboard.

This is not a cosmetic replacement for the current empty-state screen and it is not a second NEW TASK surface.

SAIHOME must become the user's glanceable command/home surface for the whole ZAICODE + SAIPEN + SAIMAIL environment:

- classic large analog clock;
- local date/time and useful calendar context;
- local usage/statistics;
- token totals and trends;
- streak/activity calendar;
- AI subscription/model limits and resets;
- prepared work / Scheduler readiness;
- active agents and autonomous runs;
- project fleet state;
- SAIPEN current work / phase / blockers / next action;
- SAIMAIL useful activity where available;
- SAIRoute / SAIFREN / SAIOPP health;
- router/provider/model health;
- recent activity;
- system health / actionable problems;
- concise useful derived metrics;
- user-configurable layout.

It must feel like the desktop/status room of the user's AI workshop.

NEW TASK remains the action/composer surface.
SAIHOME is primarily an observability, status, navigation and lightweight-control surface.

Do not collapse the two concepts.

==================================================
CURRENT MACHINE TRUTH
==================================================

Archive observed at handoff preparation:

STATE:
- phase: SCOUT
- active task: T-51
- T-51 = subscriptions as ordinary in-app chat models
- T-52 already exists in TODO and depends on T-51
- T-52 currently describes:
  - local statistics store;
  - token totals today/yesterday/week/month/all;
  - home-screen statistics;
  - Claude-Code-style activity/streak squares;
  - additional useful measures.

Relevant completed foundations:
- T-41: System Read Model / ProjectRuntimeSnapshot
- T-46: zero-setup embedded/router-owned SAIRoute foundation
- T-50: agents + Scheduler + home Scheduler readiness card
- AI limit meters already exist
- prepared prompts/schedules can highlight watched limit meters
- Scheduler knows readiness / next execution / quota reset triggers
- project/agent/queue/runtime state already has authoritative sources

Current UI contract also contains older assumptions about the home screen being a quiet empty state.
Those assumptions are superseded by this operator request where they conflict with SAIHOME.

Do not blindly bolt SAIHOME onto the old empty-state JSX.

==================================================
SOURCE / SAIPEN PROTOCOL
==================================================

Treat this handoff as a new operator requirement extending the already-planned T-52.

First:
1. reread canonical SAIPEN state;
2. reread STATE / BOARD / LOG / relevant KNOWLEDGE;
3. inspect current T-51/T-52 status;
4. register/bind the new source according to the installed SAIPEN protocol;
5. reconcile the new requirement with T-52 instead of creating a competing "Home" ticket.

Preferred interpretation:
- expand/reframe T-52 into SAIHOME + statistics;
- preserve the original statistics requirements inside it;
- do not create two independently owned Home implementations.

Respect dependency truth.

If T-51 is still active and T-52 is not eligible:
- do not steal T-51;
- do not bypass the dependency;
- leave a clean source-bound checkpoint for T-52.

If T-51 is DONE and T-52 is eligible:
- claim it canonically;
- continue autonomously through the milestones below.

Continue until:
- all eligible SAIHOME work is complete;
- or a genuine external/non-repairable blocker exists.

Do not stop after each milestone asking "continue?".

==================================================
PRODUCT CONTRACT
==================================================

The mental model must be:

SAIHOME
    "What is happening?"

NEW TASK
    "What do I want to start?"

ZAICODE WORKSPACE
    "What work/agents/tasks exist?"

SCHEDULER
    "What should start later and why?"

WORKERS
    "What execution processes are running?"

SETTINGS
    "How should all of this behave?"

Do not duplicate full editors or large configuration forms on SAIHOME.

SAIHOME may provide:
- status;
- summaries;
- drill-down links;
- compact quick actions;
- navigation into the authoritative editor.

It must not become a giant settings page disguised as a dashboard.

==================================================
MILESTONE A — FIND THE REAL HOME ENTRY PATH
==================================================

Before implementation, trace the actual current home behavior.

Known relevant locations from earlier work include, but are not limited to:
- packages/ui/src/v4/ConversationDraftEmptyState.tsx
- packages/ui/src/app-shell/WorkspaceShellLayout.tsx
- packages/ui/src/zaicode/ZaicodeSchedulerBits.tsx
- packages/ui/src/zaicode/ZaicodeWorkspace.tsx
- existing ZAICODE sidebar/navigation code
- ZAICODE settings / Layout & home
- existing engine/limit meter surfaces

Names may have moved.
Locate actual current files before editing.

Determine:
- what "Home" currently means;
- what New Task currently means;
- how startup selects a view;
- how sidebar navigation selects a view;
- where the existing Scheduler home card is rendered;
- how the empty conversation state differs from an actual application page.

TARGET:
SAIHOME should be a first-class ZAICODE view/component.

Prefer a dedicated ZAICODE-owned surface such as conceptually:

ZaicodeHomePage
ZaicodeHomeSnapshot
ZaicodeHomeLayout
ZaicodeHomeSettings

Do not keep growing ConversationDraftEmptyState into a 2000-line dashboard.

Non-ZAICODE/upstream behavior must remain isolated and unchanged.

==================================================
MILESTONE B — NAVIGATION AND IDENTITY
==================================================

Create an obvious SAIHOME entry.

Target user experience:

Sidebar:
- SAIHOME
- NEW TASK
- ZAICODE/workspace
- SCHEDULER
- other existing surfaces

Exact naming/layout should respect current ZAICODE IA, but HOME and NEW TASK must no longer behave like two names for the same thing.

Requirements:
- clicking SAIHOME always opens SAIHOME;
- clicking NEW TASK opens/focuses the task/chat composer;
- switching projects must not accidentally invoke NEW TASK;
- reopening HOME must not create sessions/tasks;
- HOME navigation has zero execution side effects;
- no "click a button to find another button" indirection.

Startup setting:
- SAIHOME
- Last active view/session
- New Task

Default for a fresh ZAICODE profile:
- SAIHOME

Preserve an existing operator preference during migration when possible.

==================================================
MILESTONE C — SAIHOME SNAPSHOT / SINGLE READ MODEL
==================================================

Do not let 12 widgets independently interrogate databases/services.

Build one assembled read projection for the home surface.

Conceptually:

ZaicodeHomeSnapshot

It should aggregate authoritative projections such as:

clock:
- current local time;
- timezone;
- date.

usage:
- token/stat aggregates;
- activity aggregates;
- collection coverage.

engines:
- visible subscriptions/pools;
- limit state;
- reset times;
- stale/fresh state;
- prepared/scheduled work.

projects:
- ProjectRuntimeSnapshot projections;
- current work;
- phase;
- blocker;
- next action;
- worker/agent counts;
- health.

agents:
- active;
- queued;
- blocked;
- recently completed.

scheduler:
- ready count;
- next event;
- watched engine;
- next reset-triggered execution.

router:
- owned/shared mode where applicable;
- health;
- SAIFREN;
- SAIOPP;
- provider/model degradation;
- latest scanner result.

messages:
- useful SAIMAIL summary if the existing APIs expose authoritative information.

system:
- ZAICODE health;
- SAIPEN capability/health;
- SAIMAIL capability/health;
- router health;
- local store health;
- update/restart state if already available.

Every value must have explicit provenance.

For time-sensitive remote/runtime values support:
- fresh;
- stale;
- unavailable.

Never silently turn:
"not known"
into:
"0".

Never present configured route/model as resolved runtime identity.

Reuse T-41's System Read Model rather than re-parsing SAIPEN files in the UI.

==================================================
MILESTONE D — REAL LOCAL STATISTICS STORE
==================================================

Implement the original T-52 requirement as a durable local statistics subsystem.

Do NOT derive long-term history by scraping rendered UI.

Record authoritative events at the runtime/service boundary.

Required core dimensions when the source actually provides them:
- timestamp;
- project;
- session/run;
- job;
- agent;
- engine/subscription;
- configured route;
- resolved provider;
- resolved model;
- input tokens;
- output tokens;
- cached tokens where available;
- total tokens;
- duration;
- terminal result;
- failure category;
- source/provenance.

Use stable event/deduplication identity.

Requirements:
- restart-safe;
- no double counting after replay/recovery;
- transactions where appropriate;
- local-only by default;
- no network telemetry introduced for SAIHOME;
- migration-safe;
- old ZAICODE profiles continue loading.

If an execution backend does not expose exact token usage:
- do not fabricate it;
- store/report coverage honestly;
- mark the corresponding metric partial/unavailable.

Example:
"2.8M tokens · 87% measured"

is acceptable if measurement really is partial.

"2.8M tokens"

is not acceptable if the missing 13% was guessed.

==================================================
MILESTONE E — TIME AGGREGATION CORRECTNESS
==================================================

Statistics periods:

- Today
- Yesterday
- Last 7 days
- This week
- Last 30 days
- This month
- All time

At minimum the UI must expose:
- Today
- Yesterday
- Week
- Month
- All time

Use the operator's system locale/timezone.

Do not hardcode UTC day boundaries.

Handle:
- DST transitions;
- timezone changes;
- midnight;
- month/year rollover;
- first day of week according to product/localization rules;
- late-arriving/replayed events.

Add focused aggregation tests for date-boundary bugs.
These bugs are boring as hell and therefore guaranteed to occur if nobody tests them.

==================================================
MILESTONE F — LARGE CLASSIC ANALOG CLOCK
==================================================

Add a genuinely attractive classic analog clock as one of SAIHOME's visual anchors.

Not a tiny icon.
Not a gimmicky digital clock wearing a circular border.

Requirements:
- large;
- classic analog face;
- clear hour/minute hands;
- optional second hand;
- tick/hour marks;
- theme-aware;
- readable at different dashboard sizes;
- vector/sharp at arbitrary scaling;
- responsive;
- does not become blurry during manual window resizing.

Prefer SVG/vector rendering unless existing architecture strongly favors another equivalent.

Clock settings:
- show/hide second hand;
- ticking vs smooth second hand where motion is enabled;
- show/hide hour numerals;
- 12/24-hour digital companion text;
- show/hide date;
- show/hide timezone;
- optional second timezone;
- seconds on/off.

Reduced-animation/global calm-interface rules:
- respect them by default;
- the clock must still show correct time;
- do not repaint/re-render the entire SAIHOME every second just because the clock moves.

Isolate clock updates from expensive dashboard widgets.

Accessibility:
- expose textual time/date;
- clock does not require visual interpretation.

==================================================
MILESTONE G — "TODAY" / AT-A-GLANCE STRIP
==================================================

The first screen should answer within seconds:

- What time/date is it?
- Is anything working?
- Is anything broken?
- What resets soon?
- What starts next?
- How much work happened today?

Create a compact Today/Now summary.

Candidate measures:

WORKING
- active agents;
- active workers;
- active projects.

QUEUE
- ready;
- waiting;
- blocked.

TODAY
- completed jobs/tasks;
- failed jobs;
- tokens;
- agent runtime.

NEXT
- nearest quota reset;
- nearest scheduled execution.

HEALTH
- healthy/degraded/blocking issue count.

The exact layout should adapt to screen width.

Do not reserve giant empty blocks when a section has little content.

==================================================
MILESTONE H — TOKEN / ACTIVITY STATISTICS
==================================================

Build the detailed local stats surface into SAIHOME.

Required headline cards:
- Tokens today
- Tokens yesterday
- Tokens 7d/week
- Tokens 30d/month
- Tokens all time

Useful supporting metrics where the data is authoritative:
- input/output split;
- cached token usage;
- turns/messages;
- completed agent jobs;
- success/failure count;
- autonomous runtime;
- models used;
- providers used;
- projects worked on;
- busiest project;
- most used model;
- busiest day;
- longest/current streak.

Useful ratios:
- completed jobs per 1M measured tokens;
- success rate;
- retry/failure rate;
- cache share;
- subscription utilization.

Do NOT invent fake "productivity" numbers.

For example:
"34 hours saved"

must not exist unless ZAICODE has an explicit defensible measurement model.

Prefer:
"34h autonomous runtime"

because that is measurable.

Costs:
- show actual billed/cost data only if authoritative;
- estimates must explicitly say "estimated";
- subscription plans without per-token billing must not be converted into fake token costs.

==================================================
MILESTONE I — STREAK / ACTIVITY GRID
==================================================

Implement a local activity grid inspired by familiar developer activity calendars.

Requirements:
- day squares;
- several months visible;
- intensity based on a selectable measure;
- current day obvious;
- tooltip with exact date + numbers;
- current streak;
- longest streak.

Measure modes:
- Tokens
- Tasks completed
- Active runs
- Agent runtime

Default:
choose the clearest reliable measure after inspecting actual event coverage.

Do not call days inactive merely because a provider did not expose token counts if other local work events prove activity.

Support:
- day/week/month zoom or range selection if cheap;
- responsive layout;
- keyboard-accessible day details.

==================================================
MILESTONE J — AI LIMITS WALL
==================================================

Bring the existing AI limit meter truth into SAIHOME.

Show all useful subscription/pool availability without forcing Settings navigation.

For each engine:
- name/account label;
- remaining/used quota according to current user setting;
- relevant windows;
- next reset;
- stale indicator;
- unavailable/sign-in-needed state;
- prepared prompt/schedule state.

Preserve the existing prepared-meter visual contract.

If an engine has work armed for its reset:
make that obvious.

Examples:
- "Prepared"
- "Starts at reset"
- "2 jobs waiting"

Click:
opens the authoritative Engines & limits / engine detail.

Do not create a second limit configuration implementation in SAIHOME.

Optional compact view:
- tile grid;
- bar mode;
- meter mode.

Use current global filter semantics.
Provide an obvious temporary "show all" view where appropriate, without silently changing saved filters.

==================================================
MILESTONE K — SCHEDULER WIDGET
==================================================

The existing Scheduler card should become a proper SAIHOME module.

Show:
- ready schedules;
- next scheduled action;
- countdown;
- trigger type;
- target project/section;
- watched engine if reset-driven;
- stop time where configured.

Include 3-5 nearest events.
Do not dump the entire Scheduler editor on HOME.

Actions:
- Open Scheduler
- Run now where semantically safe
- Pause/enable only if the existing Scheduler API already supports the operation truthfully.

Preserve exactly-once/reset semantics from T-50.

==================================================
MILESTONE L — PROJECT FLEET
==================================================

This is important for the operator's multi-project factory.

Add a Project Fleet module backed by ProjectRuntimeSnapshot.

For each visible project:
- project name;
- section MAIN0 / MAIN1 / etc where applicable;
- SAIPEN phase;
- active Work;
- owner;
- next action;
- blocker;
- active agent/worker count;
- health;
- last meaningful activity.

Visually distinguish:
- working;
- idle;
- waiting;
- blocked;
- degraded.

Do not invent state vocabulary outside authoritative runtime/protocol state.

Clicking a project:
- selects/opens that project;
- must not create a New Task automatically.

Support compact/dense view for many projects.

Target:
12+ concurrent projects must remain usable.

==================================================
MILESTONE M — AGENTS / AUTONOMY
==================================================

Add a compact "Factory" or "Agents" module.

Show:
- active agents;
- what they own;
- project;
- engine/pool;
- elapsed runtime;
- current queue state;
- health;
- next planned stop where known.

Summary:
- running;
- waiting;
- blocked;
- scheduled;
- recently completed.

Do not treat visual placement as execution ownership.
Respect the runtime-identity separation planned in T-42.

If T-42 lands before/during this work, consume its registry.
Do not create a competing worker-identity model.

==================================================
MILESTONE N — ROUTING / SAIFREN / SAIOPP
==================================================

Add a compact routing health module.

Useful information:
- router up/down/degraded;
- current owned/shared mode if meaningful;
- SAIFREN health;
- SAIOPP health;
- usable model count;
- free-model count;
- degraded providers;
- last free-model scanner result;
- last recovery/restart if useful;
- selected/default route.

Click:
open authoritative Router / Models & Routing.

If routing is healthy:
keep this compact.

If degraded:
surface the actionable fault.

Do not expose secret/API-key material.

==================================================
MILESTONE O — SAIPEN + SAIMAIL STATUS
==================================================

SAIPEN module:
- current project protocol state;
- Work;
- phase;
- blocker;
- next action;
- owner;
- verification/review state where meaningful.

For multiple projects:
show aggregated counts + allow drilldown.

SAIMAIL:
only expose information backed by an existing authoritative interface.

Useful candidates:
- unread/action-required messages;
- newest important message;
- active coordination;
- failed/delayed mailbox condition.

Do not reparse mailbox files independently if SAIMAIL already exposes a read model.

No empty decorative "SAIMAIL: nothing" rows.

Healthy emptiness should consume almost no screen space.

==================================================
MILESTONE P — ACTION CENTER / SYSTEM HEALTH
==================================================

Create an Action Center that appears primarily when something needs attention.

Examples:
- router down;
- subscription needs sign-in;
- project blocked;
- stale engine quota;
- local stats DB error;
- schedule cannot execute;
- SAIPEN unavailable;
- prepared work missed;
- update/restart needed if an authoritative updater reports it.

Show:
WHAT
WHY
IMPACT
ONE NEXT ACTION

Prefer one-click drilldown/fix when an existing safe repair exists.

Integrate Autotroubleshoot where appropriate.

Do not spam healthy green cards everywhere.
Healthy is the default; problems deserve space.

==================================================
MILESTONE Q — RECENT ACTIVITY
==================================================

Add a concise local recent-activity timeline.

Examples:
- task completed;
- agent started/stopped;
- project became blocked;
- router recovered;
- quota reset;
- prepared schedule fired;
- free model added;
- failover occurred;
- SAIPEN moved VERIFY -> DONE.

The timeline must be based on existing authoritative event sources or the new stats/event layer.

Do not synthesize events from random UI observations.

Keep default history compact.
Clicking an event should navigate to the relevant project/job/surface where possible.

==================================================
MILESTONE R — USEFUL HUMAN "NERD STATS"
==================================================

The operator explicitly wants interesting things humans enjoy measuring.

Provide useful derived facts where the raw data supports them.

Candidates:
- Current streak
- Longest streak
- Tokens today vs yesterday
- This week vs previous week
- Tasks completed today
- Autonomous runtime today
- Most active project
- Most used model
- Most reliable route
- Cache hit/share
- Runs recovered automatically
- Failed -> recovered count
- Subscription utilization
- Peak working hour
- Longest autonomous run
- Average completed job duration

All derived metrics require:
- documented formula;
- deterministic tests;
- honest "not enough data" state.

No horoscope metrics.
The dashboard may look mystical; the arithmetic must remain terrestrial.

==================================================
MILESTONE S — CUSTOMIZABLE DASHBOARD
==================================================

SAIHOME must not be one hardcoded arrangement.

Implement user-controlled layout.

Widgets should support:
- show/hide;
- reorder;
- resize where useful;
- compact/normal/large variants where useful.

Persist locally per ZAICODE profile.

Provide presets:

MINIMAL
- clock;
- Now;
- limits;
- Scheduler;
- blockers.

OPERATOR
- clock;
- limits;
- projects;
- agents;
- Scheduler;
- health.

STATS
- token totals;
- streak grid;
- charts;
- derived metrics.

FACTORY
- projects;
- agents;
- queue;
- Scheduler;
- limits;
- routing health.

CUSTOM
- user's saved arrangement.

Reset-to-default must exist.

==================================================
MILESTONE T — SMART SPACE USAGE
==================================================

The user explicitly dislikes empty wasted UI space.

SAIHOME must be responsive and space-aware.

Requirements:
- cards reflow intelligently;
- empty modules collapse;
- no giant placeholder cards;
- wide displays use extra columns;
- narrow windows stack gracefully;
- no horizontal clipping for ordinary supported widths;
- resizing must remain pixel-sharp;
- no blur caused by transform-scaling tricks;
- widgets should not overlap.

Prefer CSS grid with explicit responsive spans or an equivalent deterministic layout.

Avoid a fragile free-floating absolute-position canvas.

If implementing user drag/resize:
- use grid/snap semantics;
- persist logical grid position, not raw screen pixels;
- changing DPI/window size must not destroy layout.

==================================================
MILESTONE U — HOME SETTINGS
==================================================

Extend the existing Layout & home settings rather than creating random settings in each widget.

At minimum:

Startup:
- SAIHOME
- Last active
- New Task

Clock:
- enabled;
- size;
- seconds;
- smooth/tick;
- numerals;
- date;
- timezone;
- second timezone.

Statistics:
- enabled metrics;
- default range;
- streak measure;
- week-start convention if needed;
- retention/aggregation policy if exposed.

Layout:
- preset;
- edit layout;
- density;
- widget visibility;
- reset layout.

Refresh:
- normal refresh policy;
- manual Refresh all.

Privacy:
- local statistics explanation;
- clear local statistics;
- optional export if cheap and reliable.

Never hide destructive "clear history" behind an ambiguous reset-layout button.

==================================================
MILESTONE V — UPDATE PRODUCT CONTRACTS
==================================================

Reconcile documentation.

The old UI contract currently says things such as:
- home screen is quiet by default;
- faint Home screen link appears on hover.

That was valid for the previous empty-state design and is no longer sufficient.

Update:
- UI.md
- ZAICODE implementation notes
- architecture docs where relevant
- upstream delta ledger for touched upstream-owned files
- help/control descriptions
- settings IA

Document explicitly:

SAIHOME != NEW TASK

and identify authoritative data sources for every major widget category.

Do not leave contradictory old Home documentation behind.

==================================================
DATA VISUALIZATION GUIDELINES
==================================================

SAIHOME is information-dense but should not look like a crypto casino.

Prefer:
- readable numbers;
- subtle sparklines;
- compact bars;
- activity grids;
- meaningful status;
- restrained charts.

Avoid:
- gratuitous pie charts;
- 3D charts;
- flashing everything;
- huge gradients carrying no information;
- animations that make static numbers harder to read.

Global ZAICODE animation/calm settings remain authoritative.

Prepared work / active work may use the existing configurable highlight system.

==================================================
TRUTH / PROVENANCE RULE
==================================================

Every displayed metric must belong to one of:

AUTHORITATIVE
Directly measured/read from an authoritative source.

DERIVED
Calculated deterministically from authoritative data.

ESTIMATED
An explicit approximation with the basis documented.

STALE
Last known authoritative value, freshness expired.

UNAVAILABLE
Source cannot provide the value.

Never merge these states visually into one confident number.

Tooltips/details should expose provenance for non-obvious values.

==================================================
PERFORMANCE
==================================================

Do not build a dashboard that burns a CPU core while showing that the agents are idle.

Rules:
- clock second updates stay isolated;
- expensive stats aggregation is not recomputed every second;
- cache historical aggregates;
- event-driven updates where available;
- sensible polling for remote quota/runtime data;
- pause/reduce expensive refresh work when SAIHOME is not visible;
- no N-project × N-widget polling explosion.

With 12 projects and multiple subscriptions configured:
SAIHOME must remain responsive.

==================================================
DATABASE / STORAGE SAFETY
==================================================

If adding schema:
- use canonical ZAICODE migrations;
- additive migration preferred;
- no destructive rewrite of existing job/agent tables;
- statistics data has its own clear ownership;
- migrations are idempotent according to existing conventions;
